  "final_message": "Customers now have a `net_terms_days` setting (default 7), and finalized invoices use the customer's current value for `due_at`. The full suite passes: 35 tests, the 24 existing plus 11 new in `tests/test_net_terms.py`.\n\n- **`customers.create_customer` / `update_customer`** accept `net_terms_days`. Non-integers (including booleans) and negative values raise `ValidationError`.\n- **`POST /customers`** reads `net_terms_days` from the body and defaults to 7 when it is absent. A negative value returns HTTP 400.\n- **`invoices.finalize`** sets `due_at` from the customer's term at finalization time. Changing the term later does not alter invoices that are already finalized.\n- **Customer JSON** now includes `net_terms_days`, so the API response shows the value.\n\nI renamed the constant `INVOICE_NET_DAYS` to `DEFAULT_NET_TERMS_DAYS` because it is now only a default. Nothing else referenced the old name.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repo root. It doesn't appear in `git status`, so it is probably covered by `.gitignore`.",
